cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Predicting Judicial Support Rates in Traffic Accident Compensation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a claim-structure-driven hierarchical model for
  predicting judicial support rates in traffic accident compensation. Sixteen
  statutory compensation items are modelled separately by a pool of heterogeneous
  experts; the resulting item-level rates are aggregated to the case level using
  the case's own claimed amounts as weights, an aggregation that introduces no
  learnable parameters. A meta-learner consumes the expert predictions, their
  disagreement and the request side, and is trained with an item-balanced absolute
  error objective. The repository distributes code, configuration, a data schema
  and a synthetic demonstration dataset, but no judgment texts and no case-level
  data.
type: software
# Version of the software in this repository, matching pyproject.toml and the
# CHANGELOG. It is not a version of the manuscript.
